==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|rade||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|rode|id=ride}}, {{m|enm|rade|id=ride|t=ride, journey}}, from {{inh|en|ang|rād||riding, hostile incursion}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*raidu}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*raidō||a ride}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*reydʰ-||to ride}}. {{doublet|en|raid}}, acquired from {{cog|sco|-}}, and West Frisian {{m|fy|reed}} (paved trail/road, driveway).

The current primary meaning of "street, way for traveling"  originated relatively late&mdash;Shakespeare seemed to expect his audiences to find it unfamiliar&mdash;and probably arose through reinterpetation of {{m|en|roadway}} "a way for riding on" as saying "way" twice, in other words as a [[tautological]] [[compound]].

